{
  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5bf1012a4d4cf70aae4a1b1db2d896736fbe82332e7c6b85ca2488dcc43403ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5bf1012a4d4c-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Department of Homeland Security issued a FARO on January 26, 2021 directing Riley\u2019s removal to Jamaica."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5bf1012a4d4cf70aae4a1b1db2d896736fbe82332e7c6b85ca2488dcc43403ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5bf1012a4d4c-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Riley fled a petition for review in the Fourth Circuit three days after the FARO was issued."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5bf1012a4d4cf70aae4a1b1db2d896736fbe82332e7c6b85ca2488dcc43403ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5bf1012a4d4c-0000-0012"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Riley claimed that a powerful Jamaican drug kingpin threatened his family and that he would likely be killed if returned to Jamaica."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5bf1012a4d4cf70aae4a1b1db2d896736fbe82332e7c6b85ca2488dcc43403ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5bf1012a4d4c-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Government argued that the legal question was whether a removal order is \u201cadministratively final\u201d for detention purposes, rather than whether it constitutes the \u201cfinal order of removal\u201d for other purposes."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background and Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "case_id": "scotus-23-1270",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5bf1012a4d4cf70aae4a1b1db2d896736fbe82332e7c6b85ca2488dcc43403ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5bf1012a4d4c-0000-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court vacated the lower\u2011court judgment and remanded the case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5bf1012a4d4cf70aae4a1b1db2d896736fbe82332e7c6b85ca2488dcc43403ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5bf1012a4d4c-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Thomas, in a concurring opinion, explained that the \u201czipper clause\u201d covers CAT claims because they arise from removal proceedings, and therefore federal courts lack jurisdiction to review CAT claims unless they are reviewing a final order of removal."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5bf1012a4d4cf70aae4a1b1db2d896736fbe82332e7c6b85ca2488dcc43403ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5bf1012a4d4c-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor, dissenting, stated that Riley has received a final order of removal but never sought judicial review of that order under \u00a7\u202f1252."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5bf1012a4d4cf70aae4a1b1db2d896736fbe82332e7c6b85ca2488dcc43403ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5bf1012a4d4c-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 34,
              "start": 34
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor, dissenting, noted that an order is final for appeal when the district court disassociates itself from the case, leaving only execution of the judgment."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5bf1012a4d4cf70aae4a1b1db2d896736fbe82332e7c6b85ca2488dcc43403ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5bf1012a4d4c-0003-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor, dissenting, emphasized the \u201cwell\u2011settled\u201d presumption favoring judicial review, noting that executive determinations are generally subject to review when statutes are susceptible to divergent interpretation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5bf1012a4d4cf70aae4a1b1db2d896736fbe82332e7c6b85ca2488dcc43403ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5bf1012a4d4c-0003-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor, dissenting, pointed to \u00a7\u202f1252(a)(4), which makes a petition for review the sole and exclusive means for judicial review of any claim under the Convention Against Torture (CAT)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5bf1012a4d4cf70aae4a1b1db2d896736fbe82332e7c6b85ca2488dcc43403ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5bf1012a4d4c-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor, dissenting, argued that the law should overrule the courts\u2019 present assessment that such orders are best appealed separately."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5bf1012a4d4cf70aae4a1b1db2d896736fbe82332e7c6b85ca2488dcc43403ef",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5bf1012a4d4c-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 35,
              "start": 35
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor, dissenting, cited the foundational principle that rules of finality ensure the whole case is decided in a single appeal."
      }
    ],
