              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The Government contended that the question in Guzman\u202fChavez was whether the removal order was \u201cadministratively final\u201d for detention, not whether it was the \u201cfinal order of removal.\u201d"
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5bf1012a4d4cf70aae4a1b1db2d896736fbe82332e7c6b85ca2488dcc43403ef",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5bf1012a4d4c-0000-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Government, the Government raised practical concerns that removal orders should not become final before withholding\u2011only relief is decided, but said the Court must follow statutory text and precedent."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5bf1012a4d4cf70aae4a1b1db2d896736fbe82332e7c6b85ca2488dcc43403ef",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5bf1012a4d4c-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 13,
                "start": 13
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The Government also argued that a previously issued removal order cannot become final \u201cuntil the conclusion of withholding\u2011only proceedings.\u201d"
        }
      ],
